## Search strategy for novelty

Project keywords / canonical method names to use in queries:
{{novelty_keywords_block}}

For each of the 4 sources, run at least one `WebSearch` query covering the last 3 months. Record:
- The query string
- The source (arxiv / ccf-a-iclr-colm-tmlr / company-blogs / github-trending)
- Number of candidates surfaced
- Number actually examined (top-K)

Include these in the `Search trace` table in your report.

## Self-validation

Before returning your final sub-agent final result, verify your own report:

1. All four dimension sections present with explicit verdicts
2. Novelty section has Search trace OR is N/A with `note: search_unavailable`
3. Every CONCERN / RED-FLAG finding has non-empty `evidence:`
4. No edits to research artifacts: run `git -C {{project_root}} status` and confirm only `review/` (and possibly `cache/review/`) changed

If a self-check fails, fix the report in place and re-check. Allow ≤ 2 revisions. If the report still fails after 2 revisions, return `failed: self_validation_failed` with notes on what could not be satisfied.

## Failure mode

If you cannot produce a valid report (brief malformed, required artifacts missing, `WebSearch` unavailable AND novelty is not in `skip_dimensions`), write to `{{output_path}}`:

```
---
reviewer: {{reviewer_id}}
status: FAILED
review_ts: {{review_ts}}
failure_reason: <one-line reason>
---

# Review Report FAILED

<details: what was attempted, what blocked, what would need to change>
```

## Final sub-agent final result

Your final message to the dispatcher (one short structured block) MUST be:

```
status: pass | failed
report_path: {{output_path}}
revisions_used: <0 | 1 | 2>
notes: <optional one short paragraph, e.g., "novelty N/A because WebSearch returned no results for three sources; one source had relevant hits and was recorded">
```

Do NOT include the full report content in the notification. The dispatcher will read the file on disk.
